WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.160
So a lot of fun
went down at Kaer Morhen,

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:03.880
but it built up
to what we could call

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:05.720
the Monster Mash at the end,

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:09.040
Witchers vs basilisks
vs Voleth Ciri.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.520
Talk us through shooting
that epic fight together.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:14.360
How were the basilisks on set?

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.120
Were they just super divas?

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.360
Oh, I loved it.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.760
I loved it because you're
doing something so epic,

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.160
and you know
that it's gonna look epic.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:27.120
But essentially, you've got,
like, stuntmen in spandex

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.720
operating puppet heads,
foam puppet heads,

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.280
all in bright green.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.720
So I sometimes would giggle,

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.080
because I would catch myself
trying to be

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:40.360
all stoic and serious,
and then,

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:43.040
there's a guy in green spandex
in front of me.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:44.640
Waving his head.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.360
But then you know, like,

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:49.280
when I saw it in ADR
and I was like,

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.880
"Woo! Okay, great."

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:52.960
But it was brilliant.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.720
And, you know, long days,

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.040
but we were able to--

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:58.120
I think everybody was just
so hyped to be doing it.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.520
It was lovely.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.880
Yasen, had you ever done
that kind of fighting before?

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:03.160
-Not like that.
-Okay.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.520
Not like that.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:07.600
I remember I had a small kip

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.040
before we went to do
one of them.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.200
The first time, actually,
that they were on set, right?

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.360
-Yeah.
-And I was...I woke up,

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:17.560
and I was still in a daze,

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:19.080
and I was, like,
checks and everything.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:20.560
I walked onto set,
and like you said,

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:23.560
I just saw two, like,
green condoms just...

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:26.800
...just staring me in the face,

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:28.400
and I was still, like,
trying to just kinda

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.640
wake up a little bit.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.240
I thought, "What on earth
is going on here

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.600
with these big heads?"

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:33.960
And they were like,
"We're gonna fight that."

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.720
And I was like, "All right."

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.240
And then I said to Lambert,
"What the hell is that?"

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:38.960
He was like...

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:41.240
I just went,
"They're basilisks, Coen."

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.320
Basilisks.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:44.160
I was like, "Okay."

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:46.200
Kim, you had so many
wonderful dramatic moments

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.480
during those fight sequences.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:50.680
How do you ground yourself
in the reality of your character

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:53.280
when all these... I mean,
they are kinda silly things

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:54.800
are happening on set,

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.120
but you really have
to find your reality,

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:58.160
and these kind of
ridiculous things

00:01:58.160 --> 00:01:59.400
that the audience
will never see,

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.320
but that's what you're
experiencing as a person.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.840
How do you ground yourself?

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:04.880
I love the illusion world.

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:07.800
I love to visualize everything,

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:11.040
and they're so good today
that you can see everything

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:13.600
on iPads, what's going on.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.480
But, I mean,
you are in a room that,

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.800
as Lauren said,
is built one to one,

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:22.560
so you really get the illusion
how big these monsters are.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:25.680
Also knowing,
Lauren told me,

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.560
"We need your emotional stuff.
Come on,"

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:30.200
and you just gave me
more and more to work with,

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.760
it was, like, scary!

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:34.560
The last fight is scary,
it's so scary for me,

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.000
it's like, why?

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.600
Why didn't I see that come?

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.720
Well, it really grounds
the whole sequence.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:44.760
I mean, it's not only
spectacular visual-wise

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.200
but also emotionally.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.800
There's so many wonderful
culminations of the season.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:50.120
And we really wanted that.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:51.880
We really wanted
to put that in

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:54.720
as a statement,

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:56.840
because it's not normal
you see so much feeling

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.360
in such a big fight,
you know,

00:02:58.360 --> 00:02:59.720
because it has to go fast.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:02.600
I remember when you put it
together, and saying,

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:05.480
"These characters have to show
the emotional stuff into it,"

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:06.840
so it's like a break.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:12.600
It's like in the fight you stop time to go into our emotional stuff,

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.960
and that was incredible,
as an actor,

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.280
to have the opportunity to

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:20.400
then you couldn't let it go,
you had to follow it.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.000
It's like you're fighting
and it's going so fast,

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.400
and you really don't know
what's going on,

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.160
and then it stops,
time stops!

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:29.320
And you have all your time.

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:31.600
-It's so wonderful.
-It's so crazy good!

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:34.360
Was there a specific challenge,
Lauren,

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:37.960
in crafting that finale that
you wanna show the audience?

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:39.760
I mean, I can't imagine
it was easy in any way,

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.040
but what was
the biggest challenge?

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:44.520
Um, there were so,
so many challenges.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:46.760
I mean, COVID,
let's start with that.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:49.800
But no, I mean, I think
Kim kind of landed on it,

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:51.920
which is,
I think that so often,

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:54.120
epic battles lose
their emotionality,

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.160
and yet, what we learned,
honestly,

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.280
through our fight sequences
in Season 1,

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:00.840
is that without changing

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.480
if a battle doesn't
change a character,

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:03.960
if a fight doesn't
change a character,

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:05.320
then it's not worth doing.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:06.920
And Kim is absolutely right.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:09.280
So much of a battle
is about frenetic pace,

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:11.680
is about making sure
that it looks cool,

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:12.960
and yet, constantly,

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.840
we'd be stopping on set
to say, "No.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:17.280
We need to land on Vesemir
in this moment.

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:19.320
We need to land
on Lambert and Coen

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.160
as they're realizing
that these monsters

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.960
are coming into their home,

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:24.640
and that shouldn't be able
to happen."

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:27.480
So it really was
about timing it all out

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:29.640
and asking
these brilliant actors

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:32.960
to trust what felt like
a weird rhythm on the day,

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.440
that we would be able
to build it,

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.480
and I think, I mean, honestly,
I think it's the biggest thing

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:38.240
we've ever done
and one of my favorites.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:39.320
Like what you see?

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:40.920
Be sure to check out
the full episode

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:42.160
of The Witcher: Unlocked,

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:44.480
the official Netflix Geeked
aftershow.

